* ref3030.lib - open behavioural model of the TI REF3030E (3.0 V, SOT-23-3 series voltage reference, REF30E family).
* Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 (LICENSE beside this file), (c) the project authors.
* Clean-room model: built only from FACTS.md (datasheet facts); no vendor SPICE model was consulted.
* Provenance, every parameter's source, and the modelling choices: PROVENANCE.md beside this file.
*
* .subckt REF3030E_OPEN IN OUT GND        pin order: 1 IN (supply), 2 OUT (reference output), 3 GND
*
* Structure: an ideal source VT (3.000 V x initial accuracy, + line regulation, soft-limited to VIN - VDO, minus the
* DC load-regulation drop and a hard-ish current limit) drives OUT through the fitted output-impedance network
* ZNET (L1 || (R2+L2) || C, scaled by ZS).  IN supplies IQ plus the sourced current.  A zero-volt source VSENS
* senses the output current (positive = sourcing).  Optional noise is added in series with VT (off by default).
*
* Parameters (all FACTS rows, see PROVENANCE.md):
*   VNOM    nominal output, V                        3.0
*   ACC     initial accuracy error, % of VNOM        0      (typ; datasheet limit is +/-0.1)
*   LINE    line regulation, V per V                 16u    (typ; max is 240u)
*   LSRC    load regulation, sourcing, ppm per mA    3      (typ; max 15)
*   LSNK    load regulation, sinking, ppm per mA     3      (typ; max 150)
*   VDO     dropout, V                               0.02   (typ; max 0.2)
*   ISC     short-circuit (sourcing) limit, A        35m
*   ISNK    sinking limit, A                         35m    (modelling choice, see PROVENANCE.md)
*   IQ      quiescent current, A                     27u
*   ZS      scale of the output-impedance network    1      (1 = the 5 V part's open-output curve of Fig 6-14)
*   NOISE   1 enables the noise source               0
*   NSCALE  noise level multiplier                   1
*   NT      noise sample step, s                     2u     (transient only; bandwidth 1/(2 NT))
.subckt REF3030E_OPEN IN OUT GND params: VNOM=3.0 ACC=0 LINE=16u LSRC=3 LSNK=3 VDO=0.02 ISC=35m ISNK=35m IQ=27u
+ ZS=1 NOISE=0 NSCALE=1 NT=2u
.param RLIM=100k
.param RSRC={LSRC*1e-6*VNOM/1e-3}
.param RSNK={LSNK*1e-6*VNOM/1e-3}
* ---- output current sense (0 V): positive current flows from the network out of OUT
VSENS XO OUT 0
* ---- ideal source behind the impedance network
* a = reference incl. accuracy and line regulation (line referred to VIN = VNOM + 0.3 V); b = VIN - VDO;
* soft minimum of the two (0.1 mV knee), floored at 0
BVT VT GND V={max(0.5*((VNOM*(1+ACC/100)+LINE*(V(IN,GND)-VNOM-0.3)) + (V(IN,GND)-VDO)
+ - sqrt(((VNOM*(1+ACC/100)+LINE*(V(IN,GND)-VNOM-0.3)) - (V(IN,GND)-VDO))**2 + 1e-8)), 0)
+ - i(VSENS)*(RSRC*(0.5+0.5*tanh(i(VSENS)/1m)) + RSNK*(0.5-0.5*tanh(i(VSENS)/1m)))
+ - RLIM*0.5*((i(VSENS)-ISC) + sqrt((i(VSENS)-ISC)**2 + 1e-12))
+ + RLIM*0.5*((-i(VSENS)-ISNK) + sqrt((-i(VSENS)-ISNK)**2 + 1e-12))
+ + NOISE*V(NZ2,GND)}
* ---- output-impedance network VT -> XO, the 5 V open-output fit of Fig 6-14, scaled by ZS
L1  VT N1 {30.291m*ZS}
R1  N1 XO 1u
L2  VT N2 {9.2855m*ZS}
R2  N2 XO {46.655*ZS}
C3  VT N3 {2.8561u/ZS}
R3  N3 XO {1m*ZS}
* ---- supply current: quiescent plus the sourced current
BIQ IN GND I={IQ + 0.5*(i(VSENS) + sqrt(i(VSENS)**2 + 1e-18))}
* ---- noise: one white source shaped by H(f) = LL(f) x RES(f) + A x P(f)^2, fitted to Fig 6-13 (see PROVENANCE.md)
*   LL  lag (1+s/2pi 127.49)/(1+s/2pi 34.076)   - the low-frequency rise (a shelf of 1 down to 0.267)
*   RES 2nd-order low-pass, f0 1117.9 Hz, Q 0.9476
*   P   1-pole 2559.6 Hz, twice, weight A = -0.5318  - shallower high-frequency tail
* white density 3 uV/rtHz x NSCALE (= na*sqrt(2*NT)); the AC magnitude of VNW is that density, so an AC run with
* NOISE=1 reads the spectral density straight off V(OUT)
.param NDEN={3u*NSCALE}
.param NG={34.0758/127.4924}
.param NR1={1k*(1-NG)/NG}
.param NC1={1/(2*3.14159265*127.4924*1k)}
.param NCR={10n}
.param NL={1/((2*3.14159265*1117.9)**2*NCR)}
.param NRR={sqrt(NL/NCR)/0.9476}
VNW NW GND dc 0 ac {NDEN} trnoise({NDEN/sqrt(2*NT)} {NT} 0 0)
* path A: lag network (R1, then R2+C to ground; gain 1 at DC, NG at high f), RLC low-pass
RNR1 NW NLL {NR1}
RNR2 NLL NLC 1k
CNC1 NLC GND {NC1}
BNA NA GND V=V(NLL,GND)
RNRR NA NLX {NRR}
LNL NLX NRS {NL}
CNCR NRS GND {NCR}
* path B: two buffered poles
RNP1 NW NP1 1k
CNP1 NP1 GND {1/(2*3.14159265*2559.6*1k)}
BNPB NPB GND V=V(NP1,GND)
RNP2 NPB NP2 1k
CNP2 NP2 GND {1/(2*3.14159265*2559.6*1k)}
* sum
BNZ NZ2 GND V={V(NRS,GND) - 0.5318*V(NP2,GND)}
RNZ NZ2 GND 1G
.ends REF3030E_OPEN
